course: dictionary
lesson: 1370
title: Cantonese: a language and a place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cantonese is a language, but it can also be a describing word. The dictionary gives it two jobs: a noun for the language, and an adjective meaning from or to do with the area, its people or its food. The words around it tell you which job it has.
explain: «Many grandparents speak Cantonese, Hokkien or another dialect.» Here Cantonese names a language that people speak, so it is a noun. In «Cantonese food», the word Cantonese describes the food, so it is an adjective.
explain: «Mandarin and Cantonese sound so different that speakers can't understand each other's speech, though they share much of the writing system.» The clue is the word though: the two languages sound different, but they are written in much the same way.
fact: Cantonese is a Chinese language spoken in Guangzhou (once called Canton), Hong Kong and Macau.
fact: Many Chinese people abroad speak Cantonese, including in the UK, Canada, the USA and Australia.
fact: Cantonese is a noun for the language, and an adjective for things linked to it, such as Cantonese food.
fact: Cantonese and Mandarin sound different when spoken, but they share much of the same writing.
fact: Cantonese food includes dim sum, sweet and sour dishes and roast duck.
exercise: «Many grandparents speak Cantonese, Hokkien or another dialect.» In this sentence, what is Cantonese? | A type of food | *A language | A street in London | A kind of dance
exercise: In «Cantonese food», what job does the word Cantonese do? | A verb, meaning to cook | A noun, meaning a city | *An adjective, describing the food | A question word
exercise: «Mandarin and Cantonese sound so different that speakers can't understand each other's speech, though they share much of the writing system.» What do Mandarin and Cantonese share? | Their food | Their names | *Much of the writing system | Their cities
test: According to the dictionary, where is Cantonese spoken? | *Guangzhou, Hong Kong and Macau | Paris and Rome | Madrid, Lisbon and Dublin | Cairo and Nairobi
test: «And if Granny speaks fast, or in Cantonese or Hokkien, qǐng nín màn diǎnr shuō asks her kindly to slow down.» What does the phrase qǐng nín màn diǎnr shuō ask? | *Please could you speak more slowly | Please could you cook dim sum | Please could you tell a joke | Please could you sing a song
exam: Which of these is a Cantonese food? | Shepherd's pie | Fish and chips | *Roast duck | Porridge
